From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Build the keysym-unicode test only where there is fork()

The test splits its work among processes with fork(), which uClibc on a
system without an MMU does not have, and failed to compile there.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: not submitted

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -747,6 +747,9 @@
                c_args: keysyms_test_c_args),
     env: test_env,
 )
+# It splits the work among processes with fork(), which a system without an
+# MMU does not have.
+if cc.has_function('fork', prefix: '#include <unistd.h>')
 test(
     'keysym-unicode',
     executable('test-keysym-unicode', 'test/keysym-unicode.c',
@@ -754,6 +757,7 @@
                c_args: keysyms_test_c_args),
     env: test_env,
 )
+endif
 test(
     'keymap',
     executable(
